an implementation plan for issue #{{issue_number}}: {{issue_title}}.\\n\\n{{issue_body}}\\n\\n## Project Context\\n{{project_context}}\\n\\n## Instructions\\n1. Based on the project context, design a clear implementation approach.\\n2. List every file to create or modify with specific changes needed.\\n3. Note any edge cases, risks, or dependencies.\\n4. Keep the plan actionable — bullet points, not essays.\\n5. Follow existing patterns and conventions from the project context.\\n6. Prefer reusing existing code over duplicating.\\n\\n## Output\\nOutput ONLY the implementation plan. Do NOT write any code.\\nDo NOT open PRs, create branches, or make any git changes."}, {"id": "develop", "name": "Develop", "type": "claude_agent", "model": "claude-opus-4-6", "retry": {"max_attempts": 1}, "outputs": [{"name": "dev_result", "values": []}], "targets": ["review"], "timeout": 900, "position": {"x": 414, "y": 948}, "resume_self": true, "status_label": "developing", "prompt_template": "You are a DEVELOPER agent. Implement the changes for issue #{{issue_number}}: {{issue_title}} on branch {{branch}}.\\n\\n{{issue_body}}\\n\\n## Project Context\\n{{project_context}}\\n\\n## Plan\\n{{plan}}\\n\\n## Instructions\\n1. Implement the changes according to the plan.\\n2. Write clean, minimal code. Only change what is needed.\\n3. Follow the existing patterns and conventions.\\n4. Reuse existing code — do not duplicate.\\n5. Run tests if they exist.\\n6. Commit with clear, descriptive messages.\\n7. Push your branch.\\n8. Open a PR with .\\n\\nIf this is a retry after review feedback, the feedback is in your conversation history — address ALL requested changes, push, and update the PR.\\n\\n## Output\\nAt the end, output the PR URL on its own line."}, {"id": "review", "name": "Review", "type": "claude_agent", "model": "claude-opus-4-6", "retry": {"max_attempts": 1}, "outputs": [{"name": "review_result", "values": []}, {"name": "review_verdict", "values": ["APPROVED", "CHANGES_REQUESTED"]}], "targets": ["review_gate"], "timeout": 600, "position": {"x": 175, "y": 1120}, "status_label": "reviewing", "prompt_template": "You are a CODE REVIEWER agent. Review the PR on branch {{branch}} for issue #{{issue_number}}: {{issue_title}}.\\n\\n## Instructions\\n1. Read the PR diff and the relevant source files for full context.\\n2. Check for:\\n   - Bugs or logic errors\\n   - Security vulnerabilities\\n   - Missing edge cases\\n   - Code style consistency with the rest of the codebase\\n   - Whether tests exist and are adequate\\n   - Whether the implementation matches the requirements\\n3. Be pragmatic — do not nitpick style if the code works correctly.\\n\\nIf the code is good, respond with APPROVED.\\nIf changes are needed, respond with CHANGES_REQUESTED and list the specific fixes needed."}, {"id": "review_gate", "name": "Review Gate", "type": "condition", "branches": [{"value": "APPROVED", "target": "done"}, {"value": "CHANGES_REQUESTED", "target": "develop"}], "position": {"x": 240, "y": 1260}, "status_label": "checking review", "max_iterations": 2, "condition_field": "review_verdict", "iteration_counter": "review_round", "max_iterations_target": "failed"}, {"id": "done", "name": "Ready to Merge", "type": "end", "targets": [], "position": {"x": 120, "y": 1400}, "result_template": "Issue #{{issue_number}} implemented and reviewed. PR ready to merge."}, {"id": "failed", "name": "Failed", "type": "failed", "targets": [], "position": {"x": 360, "y": 1400}, "reason_template": "Pipeline failed after max review rounds for issue #{{issue_number}}"}, {"id": "refine_issue", "name": "Refine Issue", "type": "template", "targets": ["check_clarity"], "position": {"x": 613.9133972999781, "y": 597.4213181102986}, "template_id": 15, "status_label": "refining issue"}]}	2026-03-06 21:28:29.949563+00	2026-03-09 14:18:47.045594+00
13	Talavo Architecture Analyzer	Analyzes a specified folder in the Talavo project for code quality, deduplication, UI improvements, modernization opportunities, and bugs.	{"name": "Talavo Architecture Analyzer", "edges": [{"to": "analyze_structure", "from": "start"}, {"to": "code_quality_and_bugs", "from": "analyze_structure"}, {"to": "deduplication_analysis", "from": "code_quality_and_bugs"}, {"to": "ui_review", "from": "deduplication_analysis"}, {"to": "modernization_check", "from": "ui_review"}, {"to": "compile_report", "from": "modernization_check"}, {"to": "check_critical", "from": "compile_report"}, {"to": "create_issues", "from": "check_critical"}, {"to": "end", "from": "check_critical"}, {"to": "end", "from": "create_issues"}], "nodes": [{"id": "start", "name": "Start", "type": "start", "targets": ["analyze_structure"], "position": {"x": 0, "y": 0}}, {"id": "analyze_structure", "name": "Analyze Folder Structure", "type": "claude_agent", "model": "claude-sonnet-4-6", "outputs": [{"name": "structure_analysis", "values": []}, {"name": "structure_severity", "values": ["CRITICAL", "HIGH", "MEDIUM", "LOW"]}], "targets": ["code_quality_and_bugs"], "timeout": 600, "position": {"x": 0, "y": 140}, "prompt_template": "You are a senior Flutter/Dart architect analyzing an iOS-focused Flutter project called Talavo.\\n\\nRepository: {{repo_path}}\\nWorking directory: {{worktree_path}}\\nTarget folder/area: {{task_description}}\\n\\nPerform a thorough structural analysis of the specified folder. This is a Flutter project primarily targeting iOS.\\n\\n1. **File & folder organization** — Are .dart files logically grouped by feature? Are screens, widgets, models, services, and providers properly separated? Are naming conventions consistent (snake_case for files, PascalCase for classes)?\\n2. **Architecture patterns** — What pattern is used (BLoC, Provider, Riverpod, Clean Architecture, MVVM)? Is it applied consistently across all features?\\n3. **Dependency flow** — Are there circular imports between Dart files? Are widgets directly calling repositories or APIs instead of going through proper layers?\\n4. **Separation of concerns** — Is business logic leaking into widgets? Are StatefulWidgets doing too much? Is data transformation happening in the UI layer?\\n5. **Module boundaries** — Are feature folders self-contained? Are there cross-feature imports that break module boundaries?\\n6. **iOS-specific structure** — Is the ios/ folder properly configured? Are platform channels organized? Are iOS-specific assets and configurations in the right place?\\n\\nList every file in the target folder recursively, then analyze the structure. Provide specific file paths for every finding.\\n\\nEnd your response with a severity rating: CRITICAL, HIGH, MEDIUM, or LOW."}, {"id": "code_quality_and_bugs", "name": "Code Quality & Bug Detection", "type": "claude_agent", "model": "claude-sonnet-4-6", "outputs": [{"name": "quality_analysis", "values": []}, {"name": "quality_severity", "values": ["CRITICAL", "HIGH", "MEDIUM", "LOW"]}], "targets": ["deduplication_analysis"], "timeout": 600, "position": {"x": 0, "y": 280}, "prompt_template": "You are a senior Flutter/Dart code reviewer and bug hunter analyzing an iOS-focused Flutter project called Talavo.\\n\\nRepository: {{repo_path}}\\nWorking directory: {{worktree_path}}\\nTarget folder/area: {{task_description}}\\n\\nPerform a deep code quality and bug analysis of the specified folder. Read every .dart file and inspect carefully.\\n\\n**Bug Detection:**\\n- Null safety violations — improper use of `!` operator, nullable types not handled, late variables that may not be initialized\\n- Future/async misuse — missing `await`, unhandled Future errors, setState after dispose\\n- Memory leaks — StreamSubscription not cancelled, AnimationController not disposed, listeners not removed in dispose()\\n- State management bugs — stale state, missing notifyListeners(), incorrect provider scoping\\n- Platform channel errors — unhandled PlatformException, missing iOS method channel implementations\\n- Navigation bugs — context used after widget unmounted, Navigator stack issues\\n- iOS-specific crashes — missing Info.plist permissions, unsafe platform checks\\n\\n**Code Quality:**\\n- Widget build methods that are too long (>50 lines) or do too many things\\n- Deeply nested widget trees that should be extracted into separate widgets\\n- Business logic inside widgets instead of in providers/blocs/services\\n- Inconsistent Dart style — not following Effective Dart guidelines\\n- Magic numbers/strings that should be constants or theme values\\n- Dead code, unused imports, unreachable branches\\n- Missing or incorrect type annotations, overuse of `dynamic`\\n- Anti-patterns: setState in initState, building widgets in loops without keys, synchronous file I/O on main isolate\\n\\nFor every finding, provide:\\n- The exact file path and line number(s)\\n- What the issue is\\n- Why it matters\\n- A suggested Dart/Flutter fix\\n\\nEnd your response with a severity rating: CRITICAL, HIGH, MEDIUM, or LOW."}, {"id": "deduplication_analysis", "name": "Deduplication Analysis", "type": "claude_agent", "model": "claude-sonnet-4-6", "outputs": [{"name": "dedup_analysis", "values": []}, {"name": "dedup_severity", "values": ["CRITICAL", "HIGH", "MEDIUM", "LOW"]}], "targets": ["ui_review"], "timeout": 600, "position": {"x": 0, "y": 420}, "prompt_template": "You are a Dart/Flutter code deduplication specialist analyzing an iOS-focused Flutter project called Talavo.\\n\\nRepository: {{repo_path}}\\nWorking directory: {{worktree_path}}\\nTarget folder/area: {{task_description}}\\n\\nAnalyze the specified folder for code duplication and redundancy. Read all .dart files and compare them.\\n\\n**Look for:**\\n1. **Copy-pasted widgets** — Identical or near-identical widget trees across screens/pages. Similar Container/Padding/Column patterns that differ only in text or callbacks\\n2. **Similar widget patterns** — Screens or components that follow the same structure with minor variations (e.g., similar list pages, similar form pages, similar detail pages)\\n3. **Repeated models/DTOs** — Duplicate data classes, fromJson/toJson boilerplate that could use code generation (freezed, json_serializable)\\n4. **Repeated styling** — Same TextStyle, BoxDecoration, EdgeInsets, or Color values hardcoded in multiple widgets instead of using a shared theme or constants\\n5. **Utility duplication** — Common operations (date formatting, string manipulation, validation) reimplemented in multiple files instead of shared extension methods or utility classes\\n6. **API/service duplication** — Similar HTTP call patterns, repeated error handling, duplicate repository methods\\n7. **State management boilerplate** — Repeated provider/bloc patterns that could be abstracted into a base class\\n\\nFor each finding:\\n- List the exact .dart files and line ranges that are duplicated\\n- Show what Dart/Flutter code is repeated\\n- Suggest how to consolidate (shared widget, mixin, extension method, base class, code generation)\\n- Estimate lines of Dart code that could be removed\\n\\nEnd your response with a severity rating: CRITICAL, HIGH, MEDIUM, or LOW."}, {"id": "ui_review", "name": "UI & UX Review", "type": "claude_agent", "model": "claude-sonnet-4-6", "outputs": [{"name": "ui_analysis", "values": []}, {"name": "ui_severity", "values": ["CRITICAL", "HIGH", "MEDIUM", "LOW"]}], "targets": ["modernization_check"], "timeout": 600, "position": {"x": 0, "y": 560}, "prompt_template": "You are a Flutter UI/UX code reviewer specializing in iOS app best practices, analyzing a Flutter project called Talavo.\\n\\nRepository: {{repo_path}}\\nWorking directory: {{worktree_path}}\\nTarget folder/area: {{task_description}}\\n\\nAnalyze the specified folder for Flutter UI and UX code issues. Read all widget files, screens, themes, and styling code.\\n\\n**Analyze:**\\n1. **Widget design** — Are widgets reusable and composable? Are build() methods too large? Should StatelessWidget be used instead of StatefulWidget? Are there god-widgets doing too much?\\n2. **State management** — Unnecessary rebuilds? Is state lifted too high or too low? Missing Consumer/Selector for granular rebuilds? Are providers scoped correctly?\\n3. **iOS design compliance** — Does the UI follow iOS Human Interface Guidelines? Are CupertinoWidget alternatives used where appropriate? Proper use of SafeArea, iOS-style navigation (CupertinoNavigationBar), iOS-appropriate gestures?\\n4. **Responsive layout** — Hardcoded pixel dimensions instead of MediaQuery/LayoutBuilder? Does the layout work across iPhone SE, standard iPhones, and iPhone Pro Max sizes? Missing SafeArea for notch/Dynamic Island?\\n5. **Theme consistency** — Hardcoded colors, font sizes, padding instead of using Theme.of(context)? Inconsistent spacing that should use a design system? Dark mode support?\\n6. **Performance** — Unnecessary widget rebuilds, missing const constructors, ListView without itemBuilder for long lists, heavy computation in build(), missing RepaintBoundary for complex animations, images not cached\\n7. **User feedback** — Missing loading indicators, error widgets, empty state placeholders, pull-to-refresh, haptic feedback for iOS\\n8. **Navigation** — Inconsistent navigation patterns, missing hero animations, improper use of Navigator 2.0 or GoRouter, missing iOS back swipe gesture support\\n\\nFor each finding provide the .dart file path, line numbers, what the issue is, and a concrete Flutter/Dart suggestion.\\n\\nIf the target folder has no UI code, state that clearly and skip this analysis.\\n\\nEnd your response with a severity rating: CRITICAL, HIGH, MEDIUM, or LOW."}, {"id": "modernization_check", "name": "Modernization Check", "type": "claude_agent", "model": "claude-sonnet-4-6", "outputs": [{"name": "modernization_analysis", "values": []}, {"name": "modernization_severity", "values": ["CRITICAL", "HIGH", "MEDIUM", "LOW"]}], "targets": ["compile_report"], "timeout": 600, "position": {"x": 0, "y": 700}, "prompt_template": "You are a Flutter/Dart modernization consultant analyzing an iOS-focused Flutter project called Talavo.\\n\\nRepository: {{repo_path}}\\nWorking directory: {{worktree_path}}\\nTarget folder/area: {{task_description}}\\n\\nAnalyze the specified folder for outdated Flutter/Dart patterns and modernization opportunities. Read the .dart source files, pubspec.yaml, and any configuration files.\\n\\n**Check for:**\\n1. **Deprecated Flutter/Dart APIs** — Usage of deprecated widgets (e.g., FlatButton→TextButton, RaisedButton→ElevatedButton), deprecated methods, or packages with newer alternatives\\n2. **Outdated Dart patterns** — Old-style null handling pre-null-safety, unnecessary null checks on non-nullable types, FutureBuilder where async/await with state management would be cleaner\\n3. **Dart 3+ features** — Missing usage of records, patterns, sealed classes, switch expressions, if-case, class modifiers (final, interface, mixin class) where they would improve the code\\n4. **Flutter framework updates** — Using old Material 2 widgets instead of Material 3, missing ThemeExtension usage, old Navigator 1.0 patterns where declarative routing (GoRouter) would be better\\n5. **Dependency health** — Check pubspec.yaml for outdated or unmaintained packages, packages with better alternatives, missing null-safe versions\\n6. **Build & tooling** — Outdated analysis_options.yaml rules, missing recommended lints, outdated iOS deployment target in Podfile/Xcode config, missing build_runner or code generation where beneficial\\n7. **iOS-specific modernization** — Old iOS deployment targets, deprecated CocoaPods configurations, missing App Store privacy manifests, outdated Xcode project settings\\n\\nFor each finding:\\n- Identify the outdated pattern with file path and lines\\n- Explain the modern Flutter/Dart replacement\\n- Assess migration effort (trivial, moderate, significant)\\n- Note any breaking changes the modernization would introduce\\n\\nEnd your response with a severity rating: CRITICAL, HIGH, MEDIUM, or LOW."}, {"id": "compile_report", "name": "Compile Final Report", "type": "claude_agent", "model": "claude-sonnet-4-6", "outputs": [{"name": "final_report", "values": []}, {"name": "needs_issues", "values": ["YES", "NO"]}], "targets": ["check_critical"], "timeout": 600, "position": {"x": 0, "y": 840}, "prompt_template": "You are a Flutter technical lead compiling a comprehensive architecture review report for the Talavo iOS Flutter app.\\n\\nRepository: {{repo_path}}\\nTarget folder/area: {{task_description}}\\n\\nBelow are the results from five independent analyses of this Flutter/Dart codebase. Compile them into a single, actionable report.\\n\\n---\\n**STRUCTURE ANALYSIS** (Severity: {{structure_severity}})\\n{{structure_analysis}}\\n\\n---\\n**CODE QUALITY & BUGS** (Severity: {{quality_severity}})\\n{{quality_analysis}}\\n\\n---\\n**DEDUPLICATION** (Severity: {{dedup_severity}})\\n{{dedup_analysis}}\\n\\n---\\n**UI/UX REVIEW** (Severity: {{ui_severity}})\\n{{ui_analysis}}\\n\\n---\\n**MODERNIZATION** (Severity: {{modernization_severity}})\\n{{modernization_analysis}}\\n\\n---\\n\\nCreate a final report with:\\n\\n1. **Executive Summary** — 3-5 sentence overview of the codebase health\\n2. **Critical Findings** — Issues that need immediate attention (bugs, security, crashes)\\n3. **High Priority Improvements** — Important but not urgent improvements\\n4. **Quick Wins** — Low-effort changes with high impact\\n5. **Long-term Recommendations** — Larger refactoring or modernization efforts\\n6. **Metrics Summary** — Overall severity, estimated total issues found, categories breakdown\\n\\nRank all findings by priority. Be specific with file paths and actionable suggestions.\\n\\nEnd with an overall health rating: CRITICAL, NEEDS_WORK, FAIR, or GOOD.\\n\\nRespond with either YES or NO: are there critical issues that need immediate GitHub issues created?"}, {"id": "check_critical", "name": "Critical Issues Found?", "type": "condition", "branches": {"NO": "end", "YES": "create_issues"}, "position": {"x": 0, "y": 980}, "default_branch": "end", "condition_field": "needs_issues"}, {"id": "create_issues", "name": "Create GitHub Issues", "type": "claude_agent", "model": "claude-sonnet-4-6", "outputs": [{"name": "created_issues", "values": []}], "targets": ["end"], "timeout": 300, "position": {"x": 65, "y": 1120}, "prompt_template": "You are a project manager creating GitHub issues for critical findings.\\n\\nRepository: {{repo_path}}\\nWorking directory: {{worktree_path}}\\n\\nBased on the architecture review report below, create GitHub issues for the CRITICAL findings only. Use the `gh` CLI tool.\\n\\n{{final_report}}\\n\\nFor each critical finding:\\n1. Create a GitHub issue with a clear, descriptive title\\n2. Include the file paths, line numbers, and description of the issue\\n3. Include a suggested fix\\n4. Add appropriate labels\\n\\nCreate the issues using: gh issue create --repo {{repo_path}} --title \\"...\\" --body \\"...\\"\\n\\nList all created issue numbers when done."}, {"id": "end", "name": "Analysis Complete", "type": "end", "targets": [], "position": {"x": 0, "y": 1260}, "result_template": "{{final_report}}"}]}	2026-03-07 15:39:54.20363+00	2026-03-07 16:03:22.286682+00
15	Issue Refiner	Checks if a GitHub issue is detailed enough, and if not, analyzes the codebase and rewrites it	{"name": "Issue Refiner", "edges": [{"to": "check_quality", "from": "start"}, {"to": "analyze", "from": "quality_gate"}, {"to": "skip_done", "from": "quality_gate"}, {"to": "done", "from": "rewrite"}, {"to": "rewrite", "from": "analyze"}, {"to": "quality_gate", "from": "check_quality"}], "nodes": [{"id": "start", "name": "Start", "type": "start", "targets": ["check_quality"], "position": {"x": 120, "y": 0}}, {"id": "check_quality", "name": "Check Quality", "type": "claude_agent", "model": "claude-sonnet-4-6", "outputs": [{"name": "issue_quality", "values": ["GOOD", "VAGUE"]}], "targets": ["quality_gate"], "timeout": 120, "position": {"x": 120, "y": 140}, "status_label": "checking", "prompt_template": "You are evaluating whether GitHub issue #{{issue_number}} is detailed enough for a developer to implement.\\n\\nIssue title: {{issue_title}}\\nIssue body:\\n{{issue_body}}\\n\\nA GOOD issue has:\\n- Clear description of what needs to change\\n- Enough context for a developer to start without asking questions\\n- Some notion of acceptance criteria or expected behavior\\n\\nA VAGUE issue is missing most of the above — it is just a title, a one-liner, or lacks actionable detail.\\n\\nRespond with exactly one word: GOOD or VAGUE"}, {"id": "quality_gate", "name": "Quality Gate", "type": "condition", "branches": [{"value": "VAGUE", "target": "analyze"}, {"value": "GOOD", "target": "skip_done"}], "position": {"x": 120, "y": 280}, "condition_field": "issue_quality"}, {"id": "analyze", "name": "Analyze Codebase", "type": "claude_agent", "model": "claude-sonnet-4-6", "outputs": [], "targets": ["rewrite"], "timeout": 300, "position": {"x": 240, "y": 420}, "status_label": "analyzing", "prompt_template": "You are analyzing GitHub issue #{{issue_number}} in this repository to help rewrite it with proper detail.\\n\\nIssue title: {{issue_title}}\\nIssue body:\\n{{issue_body}}\\n\\nYour task:\\n1. Read and understand what this issue is asking for\\n2. Explore the codebase to understand:\\n   - Which files and modules are affected\\n   - What the current behavior is (if it is a bug or change request)\\n   - What dependencies or related code exists\\n   - Any relevant patterns or conventions in the codebase\\n\\nOutput a structured analysis covering:\\n- What the issue is really asking for (in concrete terms)\\n- Affected files and modules (list actual file paths you found)\\n- Current behavior vs expected behavior\\n- Key technical considerations and edge cases\\n- Suggested labels that are used in this repo\\n- Estimated complexity: small, medium, or large"}, {"id": "rewrite", "name": "Rewrite Issue", "type": "claude_agent", "model": "claude-sonnet-4-6", "outputs": [], "targets": ["done"], "timeout": 300, "position": {"x": 240, "y": 560}, "status_label": "rewriting", "prompt_template": "You are rewriting GitHub issue #{{issue_number}} to make it clear and actionable for a developer.\\n\\nOriginal title: {{issue_title}}\\nOriginal body:\\n{{issue_body}}\\n\\nCodebase analysis from the previous step:\\n{{_raw_analyze}}\\n\\nRewrite this issue with a proper, detailed description using this structure:\\n\\n## Summary\\n1-2 sentence clear description of what needs to be done.\\n\\n## Current Behavior\\nWhat happens now (if applicable, otherwise omit this section).\\n\\n## Expected Behavior\\nWhat should happen after implementation.\\n\\n## Affected Files\\nList the specific files and modules that will need changes.\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\nBulleted checklist of specific, testable criteria.\\n\\n## Technical Notes\\nImplementation hints or considerations from the codebase analysis.\\n\\nThen update the issue on GitHub:\\n1. Run: gh issue edit {{issue_number}} --body \\"<your rewritten body>\\"\\n2. Only change the title if the original is truly unclear: gh issue edit {{issue_number}} --title \\"<better title>\\"\\n3. Add the appropriate label if not already set: gh issue edit {{issue_number}} --add-label \\"<label>\\"\\n\\nThe rewritten issue must be detailed enough that a developer can start implementing without needing to ask clarifying questions."}, {"id": "done", "name": "Refined", "type": "end", "targets": [], "position": {"x": 240, "y": 700}, "result_template": "Issue #{{issue_number}} refined successfully"}, {"id": "skip_done", "name": "Already Good", "type": "end", "targets": [], "position": {"x": 0, "y": 420}, "result_template": "Issue #{{issue_number}} is already detailed enough — no changes made"}]}	2026-03-08 10:57:56.014126+00	2026-03-08 12:52:03.754972+00
