129	2	ab67a0591d47	/projects/talavo	611	Miniplayer should become a fake Dynamic Island on non-YouTube URLs	Miniplayer should become a fake Dynamic Island on non-YouTube URLs	done	\N	doohub/issue-611-miniplayer-should-become-a-fake-dynamic-	614	https://github.com/bakicelebi/talavo/pull/614	\N	0	claude-opus-4-6	0	\N	2026-03-08 14:08:55.640329+00	2026-03-08 14:16:46.460321+00	8	[{"error": null, "output": null, "status": "completed", "node_id": "start", "node_name": "Start", "node_type": "start", "duration_s": 0.0, "started_at": "2026-03-08T14:08:56.708165+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-08T14:08:56.751776+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "blocker_status=READY, blocker_reason=Issue #611 has no \\"blocked by\\", \\"depends on\\", or \\"requires\\" language in its description, and none of the open issues appear to be a prerequisite for it.\\n\\n**READY** — Issue #611 has no blockers. It can be worked on independently.", "status": "completed", "node_id": "check_blockers", "node_name": "Check Blockers", "node_type": "claude_agent", "duration_s": 10.5, "started_at": "2026-03-08T14:08:56.795644+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-08T14:09:07.262265+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "blocker_status=READY → check_clarity", "status": "completed", "node_id": "blocker_gate", "node_name": "Blocker Gate", "node_type": "condition", "duration_s": 0.1, "started_at": "2026-03-08T14:09:07.312901+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-08T14:09:07.375004+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "clarity_status=CLEAR, clarity_reason=CLEAR\\n\\nThe issue is well-specified with detailed acceptance criteria, affected files, technical notes on the two parallel systems, and concrete implementation guidance including specific method calls and state management approach.", "status": "completed", "node_id": "check_clarity", "node_name": "Check Clarity", "node_type": "claude_agent", "duration_s": 6.6, "started_at": "2026-03-08T14:09:07.424519+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-08T14:09:14.051067+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "clarity_status=CLEAR → analyze", "status": "completed", "node_id": "clarity_gate", "node_name": "Clarity Gate", "node_type": "condition", "duration_s": 0.0, "started_at": "2026-03-08T14:09:14.099531+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-08T14:09:14.143730+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "project_context=## Project Context Summary for Issue #611\\n\\n### Key Architecture\\n\\n**Two parallel systems exist:**\\n- `FloatingMiniPlayer` — bottom 64px bar, rendered inside `BrowserScreen`, shown when `dynamicIslandEnabled == false`\\n- `GlobalDynamicIsland` / `FakeDynamicIsland` — top pill, app-level, controlled via `DynamicIslandCubit`\\n\\n### Relevant Files\\n\\n| File | Role |\\n|---|---|\\n| `browser_screen.dart` (~1900 lines) | Main logic. Tracks `_videoUrl`, `_isVideoPlaying`, `_miniPlayerAnim` (300ms AnimationController 0→1). URL change callbacks at lines 1839–1452. Island calls at lines 255, 537, 571, 1179, 1188. |\\n| `video_overlay.dart` | `FloatingMiniPlayer` widget. Line 1465: skipped entirely when `dynamicIslandEnabled == true`. |\\n| `dynamic_island_cubit.dart` | `showVideoIsland(videoUrl, isPlaying)` and `hideVideoIsland()` — the control surface. |\\n| `dynamic_island_state.dart` | Stores `videoUrl`, `isVideoPlaying`, `isVideoMinimized`, `isVisible`, `isExpanded`. |\\n| `video_utils.dart` | `VideoUtils.isVideoUrl(url)` — already detects YouTube, Twitch, Dailymotion, etc. |\\n| `fake_dynamic_island.dart` | 500ms AnimatedContainer at top center. Reusable as-is. |\\n\\n### Critical Control Points\\n\\n**Miniplayer animation completion** (`_onMiniPlayerAnimStatus()`, line 250):\\n- Fires when `_miniPlayerAnim.value == 1.0` (fully minimized)\\n- If `dynamicIslandEnabled`: calls `_islandCubit.showVideoIsland(_videoUrl, _isVideoPlaying)` (line 255)\\n- **No URL-awareness here** — this is where new logic goes\\n\\n**FloatingMiniPlayer rendering** (line 1460–1473):\\n- `BlocBuilder` with `buildWhen` checking `dynamicIslandEnabled` changes\\n- Condition: if `dynamicIslandEnabled` → `SizedBox.shrink()`, else → `FloatingMiniPlayer`\\n- **No URL-awareness here** — needs to also check browser's `currentUrl`\\n\\n**URL change detection** (line 1839 `onUpdateVisitedHistory`, line 1452 `onVideoUrlChanged`):\\n- Already fires when the browser navigates to a new URL\\n- `BrowserScreen` rebuilds on tab URL changes via `buildWhen` checking `prevTab.currentUrl != currTab.currentUrl`\\n- `_videoUrl` is separate from `activeTab.currentUrl` — this distinction is crucial\\n\\n**Existing island show/hide calls:**\\n- Line 255: after miniplayer animates closed → `showVideoIsland()`\\n- Line 537: before fullscreen → `hideVideoIsland()`\\n- Line 571: video close → `hideVideoIsland()`\\n- Line 1179: drawer open → `hideVideoIsland()`\\n- Line 1188: drawer close → `showVideoIsland()` (if island enabled and minimized)\\n\\n### Key Distinction (Critical for Implementation)\\n\\n- `_videoUrl` = URL of the **video content playing** (e.g. `youtube.com/watch?v=...`)\\n- `activeTab.currentUrl` = URL the **browser tab is currently showing** (e.g. `google.com`)\\n\\nThe feature trigger is when `activeTab.currentUrl` is NOT a video URL — i.e., the user navigated away in the same tab while video is minimized. The video keeps playing but the browser is showing a non-video page.\\n\\n### What to Add\\n\\n1. **Local `_autoIslandActive` bool** in `BrowserScreen` — tracks whether the auto-island (URL-aware) is currently active, distinct from `dynamicIslandEnabled`\\n\\n2. **URL-change reaction**: In the `buildWhen` rebuild path (or `didChangeDependencies`), when `activeTab.currentUrl` changes:\\n   - If video is minimized AND `!VideoUtils.isVideoUrl(activeTab.currentUrl)` → call `showVideoIsland()` + set `_autoIslandActive = true`\\n   - If `VideoUtils.isVideoUrl(activeTab.currentUrl)` AND `_autoIslandActive` → call `hideVideoIsland()` + reset `_autoIslandActive = false`\\n\\n3. **FloatingMiniPlayer condition** (line 1468): Suppress when `_autoIslandActive == true`, regardless of `dynamicIslandEnabled`\\n\\n4. **Guard existing `showVideoIsland()` calls** at lines 255, 1188: Only call if `dynamicIslandEnabled || _autoIslandActive` (i.e., don't double-show)\\n\\n5. **Animation sync**: Reset/suppress `_miniPlayerAnim` before hiding the miniplayer to avoid a flash\\n\\n### Patterns to Follow\\n\\n- State mutations use `setState()` for local widget state\\n- Cubit calls go directly: `context.read<DynamicIslandCubit>().showVideoIsland(...)`\\n- BLoC `buildWhen` guards are used to avoid unnecessary rebuilds\\n- Existing `dynamicIslandEnabled` guard pattern is the template — mirror it with `_autoIslandActive`\\n- No new files needed — all changes are additive to existing logic in `browser_screen.dart`", "status": "completed", "node_id": "analyze", "node_name": "Analyze Project", "node_type": "claude_agent", "duration_s": 144.0, "started_at": "2026-03-08T14:09:14.186064+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-08T14:11:38.138718+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "plan=# Implementation Plan: Issue #611 — Miniplayer → Dynamic Island on Non-Video URLs\\n\\n## Overview\\n\\nAdd a local `_autoIslandActive` flag in `BrowserScreen` that activates the dynamic island automatically when the browser navigates to a non-video URL while a video is minimized. This mirrors the existing `dynamicIslandEnabled` pattern but is URL-driven rather than user-preference-driven.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## File: `browser_screen.dart` (only file that needs changes)\\n\\n### 1. Add state variable\\n\\n- Add `bool _autoIslandActive = false` alongside existing state fields (near `_videoUrl`, `_isVideoPlaying`, etc.)\\n\\n### 2. Add BlocListener for URL/tab changes\\n\\n- Add a new `BlocListener<BrowserBloc, BrowserState>` (next to the existing one at line ~1327) that listens when:\\n  - `activeTabId` changes (tab switch)\\n  - `activeTab.currentUrl` changes (navigation within same tab)\\n- Listener logic:\\n  ```\\n  if video is minimized (_videoUrl != null && _miniPlayerAnim.value == 1.0)\\n    AND !dynamicIslandEnabled (don't interfere with global setting)\\n    AND !VideoUtils.isVideoUrl(activeTab.currentUrl):\\n      → if !_autoIslandActive:\\n          setState(() => _autoIslandActive = true)\\n          _islandCubit.showVideoIsland(_videoUrl!, _isVideoPlaying)\\n\\n  else if _autoIslandActive:\\n      → setState(() => _autoIslandActive = false)\\n        _islandCubit.hideVideoIsland()\\n  ```\\n- This handles both in-tab navigation and tab switching\\n\\n### 3. Update `_onMiniPlayerAnimStatus` (line 250)\\n\\n- Change the `dynamicIslandEnabled` check to also trigger on `_autoIslandActive`:\\n  ```\\n  if (dynamicIslandEnabled || _autoIslandActive) {\\n    _islandCubit.showVideoIsland(_videoUrl!, _isVideoPlaying);\\n  }\\n  ```\\n- This ensures that when `_forwardToBrowsingTab` minimizes the video (animates to 1.0), the island appears even without the global setting\\n\\n### 4. Update `_forwardToBrowsingTab` (line 1096)\\n\\n- After the existing code, set `_autoIslandActive = true` via `setState`\\n- This preemptively flags the auto-island so the animation completion handler and FloatingMiniPlayer condition are ready\\n- The BlocListener will also fire, but having the flag set early prevents a flash of the miniplayer\\n\\n### 5. Update FloatingMiniPlayer rendering (line 1460)\\n\\n- Add `_autoIslandActive` to the hide condition:\\n  ```\\n  if (settings.dynamicIslandEnabled || _autoIslandActive) {\\n    return const SizedBox.shrink();\\n  }\\n  ```\\n- This suppresses the bottom bar when the auto-island is active\\n\\n### 6. Update `_maximizeVideo` (line 560)\\n\\n- Add `_autoIslandActive` to the condition:\\n  ```\\n  if (dynamicIslandEnabled || _autoIslandActive) {\\n    if (_autoIslandActive) setState(() => _autoIslandActive = false);\\n    _islandCubit.maximizeVideo();\\n  } else {\\n    _miniPlayerAnim.animateTo(0.0, curve: Curves.easeOut);\\n  }\\n  ```\\n\\n### 7. Update `_closeVideoPlayer` (line 568)\\n\\n- Add `_autoIslandActive` to the island hide condition:\\n  ```\\n  if (dynamicIslandEnabled || _autoIslandActive) {\\n    if (_autoIslandActive) setState(() => _autoIslandActive = false);\\n    _islandCubit.hideVideoIsland();\\n  }\\n  ```\\n\\n### 8. Update `_closeDrawer` (line 1182)\\n\\n- Add `_autoIslandActive` to the re-show condition:\\n  ```\\n  if (_videoUrl != null &&\\n      _miniPlayerAnim.value == 1.0 &&\\n      (dynamicIslandEnabled || _autoIslandActive)) {\\n    _islandCubit.showVideoIsland(_videoUrl!, _isVideoPlaying);\\n  }\\n  ```\\n\\n### 9. Reset `_autoIslandActive` in cleanup paths\\n\\n- In `_cleanupVideoWebView` (line 542): add `_autoIslandActive = false` inside the existing `setState`\\n- This ensures closing the video resets the flag\\n\\n---\\n\\n## No changes needed\\n\\n| File | Reason |\\n|---|---|\\n| `dynamic_island_cubit.dart` | `showVideoIsland()` / `hideVideoIsland()` already do exactly what's needed |\\n| `dynamic_island_state.dart` | No new state fields required |\\n| `video_overlay.dart` | `FloatingMiniPlayer` widget itself needs no changes — visibility is controlled by the parent |\\n| `fake_dynamic_island.dart` | Reused as-is |\\n| `video_utils.dart` | `VideoUtils.isVideoUrl()` already exists |\\n| `global_dynamic_island.dart` | Already renders the video island path |\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Edge Cases\\n\\n1. **Tab switching with video minimized**: The BlocListener fires on `activeTabId` change, so switching to a tab showing `google.com` activates the island, switching to a tab showing `youtube.com/watch?v=...` deactivates it\\n2. **`dynamicIslandEnabled` already true**: The BlocListener skips when `dynamicIslandEnabled` is true, so no interference — existing behavior is preserved\\n3. **Video not minimized**: The BlocListener only acts when `_miniPlayerAnim.value == 1.0`, so partially-dragged states are unaffected\\n4. **User toggles `dynamicIslandEnabled` while `_autoIslandActive`**: Reset `_autoIslandActive = false` when `dynamicIslandEnabled` becomes true (the global setting takes over). Add this in the existing `SettingsBloc` listener or in the BlocListener's guard.\\n5. **Animation flash**: Setting `_autoIslandActive = true` in `_forwardToBrowsingTab` BEFORE the animation completes ensures the FloatingMiniPlayer is suppressed immediately, avoiding a flash of the bottom bar during the transition\\n6. **Rapid navigation**: If user navigates quickly between video/non-video URLs, the BlocListener debounces naturally via setState → only the final state matters\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Implementation Order\\n\\n1. Add `_autoIslandActive` field\\n2. Update `_forwardToBrowsingTab` to set flag\\n3. Update `_onMiniPlayerAnimStatus` condition\\n4. Update FloatingMiniPlayer rendering condition\\n5. Add BlocListener for URL/tab changes\\n6. Update `_maximizeVideo`, `_closeVideoPlayer`, `_closeDrawer`\\n7. Reset flag in `_cleanupVideoWebView`\\n8. Test: minimize video → navigate to google.com → island appears, miniplayer gone → navigate back to youtube → miniplayer returns", "status": "completed", "node_id": "plan", "node_name": "Plan", "node_type": "claude_agent", "duration_s": 150.9, "started_at": "2026-03-08T14:11:38.187609+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-08T14:14:09.099226+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "dev_result=https://github.com/bakicelebi/talavo/pull/614", "status": "completed", "node_id": "develop", "node_name": "Develop", "node_type": "claude_agent", "duration_s": 118.8, "started_at": "2026-03-08T14:14:09.150767+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-08T14:16:07.983672+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "review_result=The implementation looks clean and correct. Here's my review:\\n\\n**APPROVED**\\n\\nThe PR adds a `_autoIslandActive` flag that automatically switches the miniplayer to a Dynamic Island when the user navigates away from a video URL, even if the Dynamic Island setting is globally disabled. Key observations:\\n\\n1. **State management is correct** — `_autoIslandActive` is properly set/reset in all paths: cleanup, maximize, close, and URL-change listener.\\n2. **No leaks** — `_cleanupVideoWebView` resets the flag, so it doesn't persist after video cleanup.\\n3. **`_maximizeVideo` logic is sound** — when auto-island is active and user taps maximize, it clears the flag and delegates to `_islandCubit.maximizeVideo()`.\\n4. **`_closeVideoPlayer` captures `wasAutoIsland` before cleanup** — correctly avoids reading the flag after `_cleanupVideoWebView` resets it.\\n5. **BlocListener placement is good** — listens for tab/URL changes, early-returns if dynamic island is already enabled (no double-handling), and correctly toggles the island on/off when navigating between video and non-video URLs.\\n6. **Mini player widget** — the `BlocBuilder` at line 1492 uses `buildWhen` only for `dynamicIslandEnabled`, but since `_autoIslandActive` changes trigger `setState` (full widget rebuild), the builder re-evaluates correctly regardless.\\n\\nNo bugs, edge case gaps, or security issues found., review_verdict=APPROVED", "status": "completed", "node_id": "review", "node_name": "Review", "node_type": "claude_agent", "duration_s": 38.2, "started_at": "2026-03-08T14:16:08.029767+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-08T14:16:46.263198+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "review_verdict=APPROVED → done", "status": "completed", "node_id": "review_gate", "node_name": "Review Gate", "node_type": "condition", "duration_s": 0.0, "started_at": "2026-03-08T14:16:46.316662+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-08T14:16:46.365772+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "Issue #611 implemented and reviewed. PR ready to merge.", "status": "completed", "node_id": "done", "node_name": "Ready to Merge", "node_type": "end", "duration_s": 469.8, "started_at": "2026-03-08T14:16:46.422908+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-08T14:16:46.422913+00:00"}]	\N
