26-03-08T14:09:10.845888+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-08T14:09:10.891078+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "project_context=Here's the concise project context for implementing issue #612:\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Project Context for Issue #612\\n\\n### Relevant Files\\n\\n**`app/lib/features/browser/presentation/screens/browser_screen.dart`**\\n- **Browse WebView** (`_TabWebView.build()`, lines 1627–1654): The `initialUserScripts` list includes `visibilityOverride`, `disableAutoplay`, `videoLinkInterceptor`, `colorSchemeOverride`, and conditional ad-block scripts — but **no `idleDismiss`**.\\n- **Video WebView** (lines 1796–1803): Has `idleDismiss` already injected at `AT_DOCUMENT_START`.\\n\\n**`app/lib/features/browser/data/browser_scripts.dart`**\\n- Line 449–458: Defines `BrowserScripts.idleDismiss` — no changes needed here.\\n\\n**`app/lib/features/pip/data/pip_scripts.dart`**\\n- PiP uses `pipUnblocker`, `requestPipScript`, `exitPipScript`, `pipEventListenersScript`. **No `idleDismiss` present, but the `pipUnblocker` script is only injected when PiP is enabled via the video WebView** — so the video WebView's existing `idleDismiss` covers it. No change needed here.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Coding Patterns to Follow\\n\\n- All user scripts follow the same pattern:\\n  ```dart\\n  UserScript(\\n    source: BrowserScripts.scriptName,\\n    injectionTime: UserScriptInjectionTime.AT_DOCUMENT_START,\\n  ),\\n  ```\\n- Scripts use `window.__zv_*` guards (e.g., `window.__zv_idle_dismiss`) to prevent double-injection — safe to inject in multiple WebViews.\\n- Conditional scripts use `if (condition) ...[ UserScript(...) ]` spread syntax.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Fix Summary\\n\\n**One-liner change** in `browser_screen.dart` at line 1653 (just before the closing `]` of browse WebView's `initialUserScripts`): add `idleDismiss` the same way the video WebView does at line 1800–1803.\\n\\n- **PiP**: No change needed. PiP mode renders within the video WebView which already has `idleDismiss`.\\n- **Guard**: `window.__zv_idle_dismiss` already prevents any double-injection side effects.", "status": "completed", "node_id": "analyze", "node_name": "Analyze Project", "node_type": "claude_agent", "duration_s": 77.3, "started_at": "2026-03-08T14:09:10.935693+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-08T14:10:28.195391+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "plan=\\n\\n## Implementation Plan for Issue #612\\n\\n### Change Required\\n\\n**Single file modification:** `app/lib/features/browser/presentation/screens/browser_screen.dart`\\n\\n### Specific Change\\n\\nIn `_TabWebView.build()` (around lines 1627–1654), add `idleDismiss` to the browse WebView's `initialUserScripts` list:\\n\\n- **Where:** After the last existing `UserScript` entry in the browse WebView's `initialUserScripts` array (before the closing `]`, around line 1653)\\n- **What:** Add a new `UserScript` entry for `BrowserScripts.idleDismiss` with `AT_DOCUMENT_START` injection time\\n- **Pattern:** Same as the existing entry in the video WebView at line 1800–1803\\n\\n### Files NOT Changed\\n\\n- `browser_scripts.dart` — script definition is correct as-is\\n- `pip_scripts.dart` — PiP runs inside the video WebView which already has `idleDismiss`\\n\\n### Edge Cases & Risks\\n\\n- **None meaningful.** The `__zv_idle_dismiss` guard prevents double-injection, so even if the same page context gets the script from both browse and video WebViews, it's harmless.\\n- The script runs at `AT_DOCUMENT_START`, matching the pattern used by the video WebView — this ensures it's in place before YouTube's idle detection initializes.\\n\\n### Verification\\n\\n- Play a video inline in the browse/feed tab, leave it idle — popup should not appear\\n- Play a video in the dedicated video player — should still work (existing behavior)\\n- PiP mode — should still work (covered by video WebView)", "status": "completed", "node_id": "plan", "node_name": "Plan", "node_type": "claude_agent", "duration_s": 11.9, "started_at": "2026-03-08T14:10:28.262469+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-08T14:10:40.127610+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "dev_result=https://github.com/bakicelebi/talavo/pull/613", "status": "completed", "node_id": "develop", "node_name": "Develop", "node_type": "claude_agent", "duration_s": 30.0, "started_at": "2026-03-08T14:10:40.177332+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-08T14:11:10.193377+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "review_result=The `idleDismiss` script was already present in the video WebView (line 1805) before this PR. The PR adds it to the **browse** WebView as well (line 1645). This makes sense — the \\"Video paused. Continue watching?\\" popup is triggered by YouTube's idle detection via `window._lact`, and it could appear in the browse WebView too if a video is playing there.\\n\\nLet me verify the script logic is sound.\\n\\nThe `idleDismiss` script (lines 451-458 of `browser_scripts.dart`):\\n- Uses a guard (`__zv_idle_dismiss`) to prevent double-injection\\n- Defines `_lact` as a property with a getter returning `Date.now()` and a no-op setter\\n- Uses `Object.defineProperty` to make it non-writable by YouTube's code\\n\\nThe approach is correct — YouTube checks `window._lact` to determine when the user was last active. By making the getter always return `Date.now()`, YouTube thinks the user is always active, preventing the idle popup.\\n\\n**APPROVED**\\n\\nThe change is minimal, correct, and consistent with the existing codebase. The `idleDismiss` script was already proven working in the video WebView — this PR simply extends it to the browse WebView where the same popup regression was occurring. The guard pattern (`__zv_idle_dismiss`) is consistent with all other scripts in `BrowserScripts`. No issues found., review_verdict=APPROVED", "status": "completed", "node_id": "review", "node_name": "Review", "node_type": "claude_agent", "duration_s": 35.4, "started_at": "2026-03-08T14:11:10.243529+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-08T14:11:45.642625+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "review_verdict=APPROVED → done", "status": "completed", "node_id": "review_gate", "node_name": "Review Gate", "node_type": "condition", "duration_s": 0.0, "started_at": "2026-03-08T14:11:45.689330+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-08T14:11:45.733697+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "Issue #612 implemented and reviewed. PR ready to merge.", "status": "completed", "node_id": "done", "node_name": "Ready to Merge", "node_type": "end", "duration_s": 170.1, "started_at": "2026-03-08T14:11:45.781083+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-08T14:11:45.781096+00:00"}]	\N
